  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Harvest Money Expo Scoping Study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This scoping study will give a better understanding of the needs on climate-smart and digital solutions in agriculture for the key agricultural sectors where Dutch expertise, knowledge and business cooperation could play a positive role. This will be guiding in connecting Dutch agribusinesses with the Ugandan agricultural market. The study includes an updated overview of important stakeholders that operate in the key sectors. The agricultural sector in Uganda aims to accelerate commercialization. Dutch companies could help with incentivizing the farming as a business objective by knowledge exchange and fostering business opportunities with mutual benefits. Based on the business opportunities and Ugandan agri-businesses identified through the scoping study, the project aims to help develop sustainable business relationships with Dutch businesses through field visits and matchmaking sessions organized within the framework of the Harvest Money Expo and the Netherlands agribusiness trade mission to Uganda that takes place in February 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
